Per issue #151, `TOOL_BUDGET_MESSAGE_DA` must promise nothing concrete. It may not name a channel, a time or a person. In practice that means:
- no phone number, email address or opening hour;
- none of the words `ring`, `minutter` or `timer`;
- no persona name;
- no claim to be a human, which is the EU AI Act Article 50(1) check;
- no `<` character and no digit.

The message must also be a non-empty Danish string. The string as shipped ends with "En kollega vil følge op på din henvendelse." Issue #498 (open, blocked) questions that wording because no escalation destination exists yet.
